package impl_method_ret_longer_region_under_header_bound_refused;

trait Get<'a, 'b> {
    fn get(self: &Self) -> &'b i64;
}

struct H<'a> {
    r: &'a i64,
}

impl<'a: 'b, 'b> Get<'a, 'b> for H<'a> {
    fn get(self: &Self) -> &'a i64 {
        return self.r;
    }
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    let v = 7i64;
    let h = H { r: &v };
    if *h.get() != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row impl_method_ret_longer_region_under_header_bound_refused (tier 3).
// Legal Rust: the impl method's signature need only be a SUBTYPE of the trait's; the
// return is covariant and `'a: 'b` holds in the impl header, so `&'a i64` <: `&'b i64`.
// Legality MEASURED with rustc 1.98.1 (foot of this file); compare_impl_method was the reading.
// TODAY refused: "impl Get for H: method 'get' does not match the trait declaration: the
// return type is declared '&'b i64' and the impl declares '&'a i64'". The return slot is
// compared for EQUALITY of region names, not subtyping under the impl's outlives. The
// associated-CONST twin (`const AC: Option<&'a str>` for a trait `Option<&'b str>` under
// `'a: 'b`) is admitted — there no region is compared at all. Measured 2026-09-13e on build
// 4cf0bf5e5e07b0cf (unarmed hand L_k13).
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 (round 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit, class CONFIRMED): COMPILES and RUNS exit 0. Twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/impl_method_ret_longer_region_under_header_bound_refused.rs. Audit note: rustc accepts the covariant return under 'a: 'b.
